	"_note": "No prices here: the game works out each item's Retail price live from what it costs to make (plan.md 5.12; pricing in game_config.json). An item no building makes can have a fixed \"price\" in dollars. appetite = how many of it one villager buys per hour at the Normal price in a store (plan.md 5.16). Only finished goods have one, so raw goods like Wheat can't be sold in shops (the Trading Post buys anything, plan.md 5.22). category = what kind of item it is (names in game_config.json item_categories): stores sell the categories in their \"sells\" list, and the Food need counts only \"food\". Appetites are PLACEHOLDERS: Flour and Bread are tuned so about 40 people buy what one Farm + Mill + Bakery make; the Wave 1 foods (plan.md 5.21) so about 100 people buy what one building makes in an hour. Not realistic amounts: the game only shows village totals.",
